☸️ Top 20 Kubernetes Scenario-Based Interview Questions
Senior Java Developer (Spring Boot + AWS EKS)
1. Spring Boot Pod Crashes Repeatedly
Scenario
Pod Status:

CrashLoopBackOff

What Will You Check?
kubectl logs pod-name

kubectl describe pod pod-name


Check:

Application Error

Memory Issue

Database Connectivity

Environment Variables

Interview One-Liner
Always check logs first, then events.

2. Pod Stuck In Pending
Scenario
Pod Never Starts.

Checks
kubectl describe pod pod-name


Possible Reasons:

No Available CPU

No Available Memory

Node Selector Mismatch

Taints/Tolerations

One-Liner
Pending means Kubernetes cannot schedule the Pod.

3. What Happens If Pod Crashes?
Flow
Pod Dies
    ↓
Deployment Detects
    ↓
ReplicaSet Creates New Pod

One-Liner
Deployments provide self-healing.

4. Difference Between Pod and Deployment
Pod
Single Instance

Deployment
Manages Pods

Scaling

Rolling Updates

Self Healing

One-Liner
Never deploy production applications using bare Pods.

5. High Traffic Suddenly Comes
Scenario

Traffic increases from:

500 TPS

to

5000 TPS

Solution
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler

minReplicas: 2
maxReplicas: 10

One-Liner
Use HPA to scale Pods automatically.

6. Health Endpoint Down
Scenario

Application Running

But Traffic Should Stop

Solution
readinessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/readiness

One-Liner
Readiness controls traffic.

7. Application Hung
Scenario

App is alive but stuck forever.

Solution
livenessProbe:
  httpGet:
    path: /actuator/health/liveness

Flow
Probe Fails
   ↓
Pod Restarted

One-Liner
Liveness restarts unhealthy Pods.

8. Store Passwords?
Wrong
ConfigMap

Correct
Secret


Example

secretKeyRef:
  name: db-secret

One-Liner
ConfigMap = Non Sensitive

Secret = Sensitive

9. Pod Can Start But Cannot Reach Database
Checks
kubectl exec -it pod-name -- sh


Check

DNS

Network

Security Groups

Network Policies

One-Liner
Always verify pod-to-service connectivity.

10. Difference Between Service and Ingress
Service
Expose Pods

Ingress
Expose URL


Flow

Internet
   ↓
Ingress
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Pods

One-Liner
Ingress routes traffic, Service connects Pods.

11. User Gets 503 Error
Check
kubectl get endpoints

kubectl get pods


Possible Reasons

Pods Not Ready

No Endpoints

Readiness Probe Failure

One-Liner
503 usually means Service has no healthy backend Pods.

12. Rolling Deployment
Scenario

Deploy New Version Without Downtime

kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml


Flow

Old Pod
    ↓
New Pod Created
    ↓
Traffic Shifted

One-Liner
Deployments support rolling updates automatically.

13. Rollback Deployment
Command
kubectl rollout undo deployment payment-service

One-Liner
Deployment history allows quick rollback.

14. Node Fails
Scenario

Worker Node Goes Down

Flow
Node Down
     ↓
Pods Lost
     ↓
Scheduler Creates Pods
     ↓
Healthy Nodes

One-Liner
Kubernetes reschedules workloads automatically.

15. Stateful Application Deployment
Scenario

Deploy Kafka

Deploy Oracle

Deploy PostgreSQL

Use?

StatefulSet

Why?
Stable Hostname

Persistent Storage

Stable Identity

One-Liner
Stateful workloads require StatefulSets.

16. Persistent Data Lost
Cause

Using

emptyDir

Solution
PersistentVolumeClaim

One-Liner
Pod restart can destroy local storage.

17. OOMKilled
Scenario
Pod Restarting

Status = OOMKilled

Fix
resources:
  requests:
    memory: "512Mi"

  limits:
    memory: "1Gi"

One-Liner
OOMKilled means the container exceeded memory limits.

18. Restrict One Pod From Accessing Others
Use
kind: NetworkPolicy

Example
podSelector:
   matchLabels:
      app: payment

One-Liner
Network Policies control pod-to-pod traffic.

19. How To Debug Production Pod?
Commands
kubectl get pods

kubectl describe pod pod-name

kubectl logs pod-name

kubectl top pod

One-Liner
Describe → Logs → Metrics is the usual troubleshooting order.

20. Design Banking Payment Service On Kubernetes
Architecture
Internet
    ↓
Ingress
    ↓
Service
    ↓
Payment Pods (3 Replicas)
    ↓
Kafka
    ↓
Database

Add
HPA

ConfigMap

Secrets

Liveness Probe

Readiness Probe

PVC

Monitoring

One-Liner
Production Kubernetes design focuses on scalability, resiliency, security and observability.

